WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.929
The Azure collector
makes two declared calls:

2
00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:06.112
the events query and the
impacted-resources query.

3
00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:11.162
Each is an Azure Resource Graph query in
live mode, and a file in fixture mode.

4
00:00:11.162 --> 00:00:13.962
Then it maps each event type to a kind.

5
00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:15.826
Service issues are incidents.

6
00:00:15.826 --> 00:00:17.975
Planned maintenance is maintenance.

7
00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:22.361
A health advisory whose event subtype
is Retirement is a retirement,

8
00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:24.901
and it's action required
by the kit's rule,

9
00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:29.287
due at the advisory's end time, which
Learn says is its mitigation time.

10
00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:31.988
Any other health advisory is an advisory.

11
00:00:31.988 --> 00:00:36.316
A security advisory is action
required by the kit's rule,

12
00:00:36.316 --> 00:00:38.951
with no date, for the ISSO to review.

13
00:00:38.951 --> 00:00:42.937
And anything else, such as
billing, is left out and counted.

14
00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:47.788
Resources come from the impacted-resources
rows with the same tracking I D.

15
00:00:47.788 --> 00:00:52.251
The source link is the event on the
cloud's own Resource Manager host.

16
00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.750
An unknown cloud name
throws; there is no default.
